#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:2
msgid "The calibre Content server"
msgstr "Calibreov server sadržaja"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:4
msgid ""
"The calibre :guilabel:`Content server` allows you to access your calibre "
"libraries and read books directly in a browser on your favorite mobile phone"
" or tablet device. As a result, you do not need to install any dedicated "
"book reading/management apps on your phone. Just use the browser. The server"
" downloads and stores the book you are reading in an off-line cache so that "
"you can read it even when there is no internet connection."
msgstr "Calibre :guilabel:`Content server` vam omogućava da pristupite svojim calibre bibliotekama i čitate knjige direktno u pregledaču na vašem omiljenom mobilnom telefonu ili tabletu. Zbog toga ne morate da instalirate nikakve posebne aplikacije za čitanje/upravljanje knjigama na telefonu. Samo koristite pregledač. Server preuzima i čuva knjigu koju čitate u oflajn kešu tako da možete da je čitate čak i kada nema internet veze."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:13
msgid "Contents"
msgstr "Sadržaj"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:15
msgid ""
"To start the server, click the :guilabel:`Connect/share` button and choose "
":guilabel:`Start Content server`. You might get a message from your "
"computer's firewall or anti-virus program asking if it is OK to allow access"
" to ``calibre.exe``. Click the ``Allow`` or ``OK`` button.  Then open a "
"browser (preferably Chrome or Firefox) in your computer and type in the "
"following address:"
msgstr "Da biste pokrenuli server, kliknite na dugme :guilabel:`Connect/share` i izaberite :guilabel:`Start Content server`. Možda ćete dobiti poruku od zaštitnog zida vašeg računara ili antivirusnog programa sa pitanjem da li je u redu dozvoliti pristup za ``calibre.exe``. Kliknite na dugme ``Allow`` ili ``OK``. Zatim otvorite pregledač (po mogućstvu Chrome ili Firefox) na vašem računaru i ukucajte sledeću adresu:"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:22
msgid "http://127.0.0.1:8080"
msgstr "http://127.0.0.1:8080"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:24
msgid ""
"This will open a page in the browser showing you your calibre libraries, "
"click on any one and browse the books in it. Click on a book, and it will "
"show you all the metadata about the book, along with buttons to "
":guilabel:`Read` and :guilabel:`Download` the book. Click the "
":guilabel:`Read` button to start reading the book."
msgstr "Otvoriće se stranica s vašim calibre bibliotekama. Izaberite neku od njih i pregledajte knjige u njoj. Kliknite na knjigu i prikazaće vam se svi metapodaci o knjizi, zajedno sa dugmadima za :guilabel:`Read` i :guilabel:`Download` knjige. Kliknite na dugme :guilabel:`Read` da biste počeli da čitate knjigu."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:30
msgid ""
"The address used above ``http://127.0.0.1:8080`` will only work on the "
"computer that is running calibre. To access the server from other "
"computers/phones/tablets/etc. you will need to do a little more work, as "
"described in the next section."
msgstr "Adresa korišćena iznad ``http://127.0.0.1:8080`` će raditi samo na računaru na kojem je pokrenut calibre. Da biste pristupili serveru sa drugih računara/telefona/tableta/itd. moraćete da uradite malo više posla, kao što je opisano u sledećem odeljku."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:37
msgid "Accessing the Content server from other devices"
msgstr "Pristupanje Content serveru sa drugih uređaja"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:39
msgid ""
"There are two types of remote device access that you will typically need. "
"The first, simpler kind is from within your home network. If you are running"
" calibre on a computer on your home network and you have also connected your"
" other devices to the same home network, then you should be easily able to "
"access the server on those devices."
msgstr "Obično će vam trebati dve vrste pristupa s drugih uređaja. Prva, jednostavnija vrsta je iz vaše kućne mreže. Ako pokrećete calibre na računaru u vašoj kućnoj mreži i takođe ste povezali vaše druge uređaje na istu kućnu mrežu, onda bi trebalo da lako možete da pristupite serveru na tim uređajima."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:46
msgid "Accessing the server from devices on your home network"
msgstr "Pristupanje serveru sa uređaja u vašoj kućnoj mreži"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:48
msgid ""
"After starting the server in calibre as described above, click the "
":guilabel:`Connect/share` button again. Instead of the :guilabel:`Start "
"Content server` action, you should see a :guilabel:`Stop Content server` "
"action instead. To the right of this action will be listed an IP address and"
" port number. These look like a bunch of numbers separated by periods. For "
"example::"
msgstr "Nakon pokretanja servera u calibre-u kao što je gore opisano, ponovo kliknite na dugme :guilabel:`Connect/share`. Umesto akcije :guilabel:`Start Content server`, trebalo bi da vidite akciju :guilabel:`Stop Content server`. Desno od ove akcije biće navedena IP adresa i broj porta. Oni izgledaju kao niz brojeva razdvojenih tačkama. Na primer::"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:57
msgid ""
"These numbers tell you what address to use to connect to the server in your "
"devices. Following the example above, the address becomes::"
msgstr "Ovi brojevi vam govore koju adresu da koristite za povezivanje sa serverom na vašim uređajima. Prateći gornji primer, adresa postaje::"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:62
msgid ""
"The first part of the address is always ``http://`` the next part is the IP "
"address, which is the numbers before the comma and finally we have the port "
"number which must be added to the IP address with a colon (``:``). If you "
"are lucky, that should be all you need and you will be looking at the "
"calibre libraries on your device. If not, read on."
msgstr "Prvi deo adrese je uvek ``http://``, sledeći deo je IP adresa, što su brojevi pre zareza, i na kraju imamo broj porta koji se mora dodati IP adresi sa dvotačkom (``:``). Ako imate sreće, to bi trebalo da bude sve što vam treba i gledaćete calibre biblioteke na vašem uređaju. Ako ne, čitajte dalje."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:70
msgid "Trouble-shooting the home network connection"
msgstr "Rešavanje problema sa vezom na kućnoj mreži"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:72
msgid ""
"If you are unable to access the server from your device, try the following "
"steps:"
msgstr "Ako ne možete da pristupite serveru sa vašeg uređaja, pokušajte sledeće korake:"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:75
msgid ""
"Check that the server is running by opening the address "
"``http://127.0.0.1:8080`` in a browser running on the same computer as the "
"server."
msgstr "Proverite da li server radi otvaranjem adrese ``http://127.0.0.1:8080`` u pregledaču koji radi na istom računaru kao i server."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:79
msgid ""
"Check that your firewall/anti-virus is allowing connections to your computer"
" on the port ``8080`` and to the calibre program. The easiest way to "
"eliminate the firewall/anti-virus as the source of problems is to "
"temporarily turn them both off and then try connecting. You should first "
"disconnect from the internet, before turning off the firewall, to keep your "
"computer safe."
msgstr "Proverite da li vaš zaštitni zid/antivirus dozvoljava veze sa vašim računarom na portu ``8080`` i sa programom calibre. Najlakši način da eliminišete zaštitni zid/antivirus kao izvor problema je da ih privremeno isključite i zatim pokušate da se povežete. Trebalo bi prvo da se isključite sa interneta, pre nego što isključite zaštitni zid, kako biste zaštitili svoj računar."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:86
msgid ""
"Check that your device and computer are on the same network. This means they"
" should both be connected to the same wireless router. In particular neither"
" should be using a cellular or ISP provided direct-WiFi connection."
msgstr "Proverite da li su vaš uređaj i računar na istoj mreži. To znači da bi oba trebalo da budu povezana na isti bežični ruter. Konkretno, nijedan ne bi trebalo da koristi mobilnu ili direktnu WiFi vezu koju obezbeđuje ISP."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:90
msgid ""
"If you have non-standard networking setup, it might be that the IP address "
"shown on the :guilabel:`Connect/share` menu is incorrect. In such a case you"
" will have to figure out what the correct IP address to use is, yourself. "
"Unfortunately, given the infinite diversity of network configurations "
"possible, it is not possible to give you a roadmap for doing so."
msgstr "Ako imate nestandardno mrežno podešavanje, može se desiti da je IP adresa prikazana u meniju :guilabel:`Connect/share` netačna. U tom slučaju ćete morati sami da otkrijete koja je ispravna IP adresa. Nažalost, s obzirom na beskonačnu raznolikost mogućih mrežnih konfiguracija, nije moguće dati vam uputstvo kako to da uradite."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:97
msgid ""
"If you have set up a username and password, first try it without that to see"
" if it is causing issues. Some e-ink devices have browsers that do not "
"handle authentication. You can sometimes workaround this by including the "
"username and password in the URL, for example: "
"``http://username:password@192.168.1.2:8080``."
msgstr "Ako ste postavili korisničko ime i lozinku, prvo pokušajte bez toga da vidite da li to izaziva probleme. Neki e-ink uređaji imaju pregledače koji ne podržavaju autentifikaciju. Ponekad to možete zaobići uključivanjem korisničkog imena i lozinke u URL, na primer: ``http://username:password@192.168.1.2:8080``."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:103
msgid ""
"If you are stuck, you can always ask for help in the `calibre user forums`_."
msgstr "Ako vam zatreba pomoć, možete je potražiti na `calibre user forums`_."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:107
msgid "Accessing the server from anywhere on the internet"
msgstr "Pristupanje serveru sa bilo kog mesta na internetu"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:111
msgid ""
"Before doing this you should turn on username/password protection in the "
"server, otherwise anyone in the world will be able to access your books. Go "
"to :guilabel:`Preferences->Sharing->Sharing over the net` and enable the "
"option to :guilabel:`Require username and password to access the content "
"server`."
msgstr "Pre nego što ovo uradite, trebalo bi da uključite zaštitu korisničkim imenom/lozinkom na serveru, inače će svako na svetu moći da pristupi vašim knjigama. Idite na :guilabel:`Preferences->Sharing->Sharing over the net` i omogućite opciju :guilabel:`Require username and password to access the content server`."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:117
msgid ""
"While the particular details on setting up internet access vary depending on"
" the network configuration and type of computer you are using, the basic "
"schema is as follows."
msgstr "Iako se određeni detalji o postavljanju pristupa internetu razlikuju u zavisnosti od mrežne konfiguracije i tipa računara koji koristite, osnovna šema je sledeća."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:121
msgid ""
"Find out the external IP address of the computer you are going to run the "
"server on. You can do that by visiting the site `What is my IP address "
"<https://www.whatismyip.com/>`_ in a browser running on the computer."
msgstr "Saznajte spoljnu IP adresu računara na kojem ćete pokrenuti server. To možete uraditi posetom sajtu `What is my IP address <https://www.whatismyip.com/>`_ u pregledaču koji radi na tom računaru."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:125
msgid ""
"If the computer is behind a router, enable port forwarding on the router to "
"forward the port ``8080`` (or whatever port you choose to run the calibre "
"Content server on) to the computer."
msgstr "Ako je računar iza rutera, omogućite prosleđivanje portova na ruteru kako biste prosledili port ``8080`` (ili bilo koji port koji izaberete za pokretanje calibre Content servera) na računar."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:129
msgid ""
"Make sure the calibre server is allowed through any firewalls/anti-virus "
"programs on your computer."
msgstr "Proverite da li je calibre server dozvoljen kroz sve zaštitne zidove/antivirusne programe na vašem računaru."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:132
msgid ""
"Now you should be able to access the server on any internet-connected device"
" using the IP address you found in the first step. For example, if the IP "
"address you found was ``123.123.123.123`` and the port you are using for the"
" calibre server is ``8080``, the address to use on your device becomes: "
"``http://123.123.123.123:8080``."
msgstr "Sada bi trebalo da možete da pristupite serveru na bilo kom uređaju povezanom na internet koristeći IP adresu koju ste pronašli u prvom koraku. Na primer, ako je IP adresa koju ste pronašli bila ``123.123.123.123``, a port koji koristite za calibre server je ``8080``, adresa koju treba koristiti na vašem uređaju postaje: ``http://123.123.123.123:8080``."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:138
msgid ""
"Optionally, use a service like `no-ip <https://www.noip.com/free>`_ to setup"
" an easy to remember address to use instead of the IP address you found in "
"the first step."
msgstr "Opciono, koristite uslugu kao što je `no-ip <https://www.noip.com/free>`_ da biste postavili adresu koja se lako pamti umesto IP adrese koju ste pronašli u prvom koraku."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:146
msgid ""
"For maximum security, you should also enable HTTPS on the Content server. "
"You can either do so directly in the server by providing the path to the "
"HTTPS certificate to use in the advanced configuration options for the "
"server, or you can set up a reverse proxy as described below, to use an "
"existing HTTPS setup."
msgstr "Za maksimalnu bezbednost, takođe bi trebalo da omogućite HTTPS na Content serveru. To možete učiniti direktno na serveru tako što ćete navesti putanju do HTTPS sertifikata koji će se koristiti u naprednim opcijama konfiguracije za server, ili možete postaviti obrnuti proksi kao što je opisano u nastavku, da biste koristili postojeću HTTPS postavku."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:154
msgid "The server interface"
msgstr "Interfejs servera"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:156
msgid ""
"The server interface is a simplified version of the main calibre interface, "
"optimised for use with touch screens. The home screen shows you books you "
"are currently reading as well as allowing you to choose a calibre library "
"you want to browse. The server in calibre gives you access to all your "
"libraries, not just a single one, as before."
msgstr "Interfejs servera je pojednostavljena verzija glavnog calibre interfejsa, optimizovana za upotrebu sa ekranima osetljivim na dodir. Početni ekran vam prikazuje knjige koje trenutno čitate, kao i omogućava vam da izaberete calibre biblioteku koju želite da pregledate. Server u calibre-u vam daje pristup svim vašim bibliotekama, a ne samo jednoj, kao ranije."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:163
msgid "The book list"
msgstr "Lista knjiga"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:165
msgid ""
"The server book list is a simple grid of covers. Tap on a cover to see the "
"detailed metadata for a book, or to read the book. If you prefer a more "
"detailed list, you can change the default view by clicking the three "
"vertical dots in the top right corner."
msgstr "Lista knjiga na serveru je jednostavna mreža korica. Dodirnite koricu da biste videli detaljne metapodatke za knjigu ili da biste pročitali knjigu. Ako više volite detaljniju listu, možete promeniti podrazumevani prikaz klikom na tri vertikalne tačke u gornjem desnom uglu."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:170
msgid ""
"Sorting and searching of the book list should be familiar to calibre users. "
"They can be accessed by clicking their icons in the top right area. They "
"both work exactly the same as in the main calibre program. The search page "
"even allows you to construct search queries by clicking on "
"authors/tags/etc., just as you can using the Tag browser in the main "
"program."
msgstr "Sortiranje i pretraživanje liste knjiga bi trebalo da bude poznato korisnicima calibre-a. Može im se pristupiti klikom na njihove ikone u gornjem desnom uglu. Oba rade potpuno isto kao u glavnom programu calibre. Stranica za pretragu vam čak omogućava da konstruišete upite za pretragu klikom na autore/oznake/itd., baš kao što možete koristeći Pregledač oznaka u glavnom programu."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:176
msgid ""
"A much loved feature of the main program, :guilabel:`Virtual libraries` is "
"present in the server interface as well. Click the three vertical dots in "
"the top right corner to choose a Virtual library."
msgstr "Veoma voljena funkcija glavnog programa, :guilabel:`Virtual libraries` je takođe prisutna u interfejsu servera. Kliknite na tri vertikalne tačke u gornjem desnom uglu da izaberete Virtuelnu biblioteku."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:181
msgid "The book viewer"
msgstr "Pregledač knjiga"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:183
msgid ""
"You can read any book in your calibre library by simply tapping on it and "
"then tapping the :guilabel:`Read` button. The book viewer is very simple to "
"operate. You can both tap and swipe to turn pages. Swiping up/down skips "
"between chapters. Tapping the top quarter of the screen gets you the "
"detailed controls and viewer preferences."
msgstr "Možete čitati bilo koju knjigu u vašoj calibre biblioteci jednostavnim dodirom na nju, a zatim dodirom na dugme :guilabel:`Read`. Pregledač knjiga je veoma jednostavan za korišćenje. Možete i dodirnuti i prevući da biste okrenuli stranice. Prevlačenje gore/dole preskače između poglavlja. Dodirivanjem gornje četvrtine ekrana dobijate detaljne kontrole i podešavanja pregledača."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:189
msgid ""
"If you leave the Content server running, you can even open the same book on "
"multiple devices and it will remember your last read position. If it does "
"not you can force a sync by tapping in the top quarter and choosing "
":guilabel:`Sync`."
msgstr "Ako ostavite Content server da radi, možete čak otvoriti istu knjigu na više uređaja i on će zapamtiti vašu poslednju pročitanu poziciju. Ako to ne učini, možete forsirati sinhronizaciju dodirom u gornjoj četvrtini i biranjem :guilabel:`Sync`."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:195
msgid "Searching book contents in OPDS applications"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:197
msgid ""
"When full text indexing is enabled for a library, its OPDS catalog offers a "
"catalog entry titled :guilabel:`Search book contents`. Open this entry and "
"use the application's search control to find books by words and phrases "
"inside them, using calibre's existing full text index. Each feed has a "
"single search link, so clients do not have to choose between multiple search"
" links. Results contain the normal book information and download links. A "
"book is listed once even if more than one of its formats matches. Only books"
" available to the current user are searched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:206
msgid ""
"The original search continues to search book metadata. Content search uses "
"the same SQLite full text query syntax as calibre's full text search window."
" It searches the text indexed so far; books still waiting to be indexed will"
" not appear yet. The content search entry is absent when indexing is "
"disabled. Both OPDS 1 and OPDS 2 catalogs support content search, through "
"the normal search URL with ``full_text=y`` added to its query parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:215
msgid "Reading comics in OPDS applications"
msgstr "Čitanje stripova u OPDS aplikacijama"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:217
msgid ""
"Applications that support OPDS 2.0 and the `Readium Divina format "
"<https://readium.org/webpub-manifest/profiles/divina>`_ can read CBZ comics "
"one page at a time, without downloading the entire archive. Connect the "
"application to the server's ``/opds`` catalog. OPDS 2.0 applications request"
" the JSON catalog using ``Accept: application/opds+json``."
msgstr "Aplikacije koje podržavaju OPDS 2.0 i `format Readium Divina <https://readium.org/webpub-manifest/profiles/divina>`_ mogu čitati CBZ stripove stranicu po stranicu, bez preuzimanja cele arhive. Povežite aplikaciju sa katalogom ``/opds`` na serveru. OPDS 2.0 aplikacije zahtevaju JSON katalog pomoću zaglavlja ``Accept: application/opds+json``."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:223
msgid ""
"Comic entries link to a Divina manifest. The server lists pages only when "
"the application opens that manifest, using the same page order as calibre's "
"comic conversion. Each page offers its original image format, including AVIF"
" and JPEG XL, and alternate formats the server can produce. GIF pages, which"
" may be animated, are only offered in their original format. The application"
" chooses an image format it supports from those links. JPEG is offered as "
"the default for AVIF and JPEG XL pages when conversion is available."
msgstr "Stavke stripova sadrže vezu ka Divina manifestu. Server prikazuje listu stranica tek kada aplikacija otvori taj manifest, koristeći isti redosled stranica kao pri pretvaranju stripova u calibre-u. Za svaku stranicu ponuđeni su njen izvorni format slike, uključujući AVIF i JPEG XL, i alternativni formati koje server može da napravi. GIF stranice, koje mogu biti animirane, nude se samo u izvornom formatu. Aplikacija iz ponuđenih veza bira format slike koji podržava. JPEG se nudi kao podrazumevani format za AVIF i JPEG XL stranice kada je pretvaranje dostupno."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:231
msgid ""
"For manga, a ``ComicInfo.xml`` file with ``Manga`` set to "
"``YesAndRightToLeft`` tells the application to use right-to-left reading "
"direction. The file can be in the root of the archive or in the folder "
"containing the page images. Page images remain in their original order. The "
"reading direction is only given in the comic manifest, not in OPDS feeds, as"
" finding it requires opening the archive."
msgstr "Za mange, datoteka ``ComicInfo.xml`` sa svojstvom ``Manga`` postavljenim na ``YesAndRightToLeft`` govori aplikaciji da koristi smer čitanja zdesna nalevo. Datoteka se može nalaziti u korenu arhive ili u fascikli koja sadrži slike stranica. Slike stranica ostaju u izvornom redosledu. Smer čitanja navodi se samo u manifestu stripa, a ne u OPDS izvorima, jer je za njegovo utvrđivanje potrebno otvoriti arhivu."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:238
msgid ""
"The normal username/password and library restrictions apply to manifests and"
" page images. Complete archive downloads remain available. This feature "
"supports CBZ archives; CBR and CB7 comics can still be downloaded as "
"complete files."
msgstr "Uobičajena ograničenja u vezi sa korisničkim imenom, lozinkom i bibliotekama važe i za manifeste i slike stranica. Preuzimanje celih arhiva i dalje je dostupno. Ova funkcija podržava CBZ arhive; CBR i CB7 stripovi i dalje se mogu preuzeti kao cele datoteke."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:244
msgid "Browser support"
msgstr "Podrška za pregledače"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:246
msgid ""
"The new calibre server makes lots of use of advanced HTML 5 and CSS 3 "
"features. As such it requires an up-to-date browser to use. It has been "
"tested on Android Chrome and iOS Safari as well as Chrome and Firefox on the"
" desktop."
msgstr "Novi calibre server u velikoj meri koristi napredne HTML 5 i CSS 3 funkcije. Kao takav, zahteva ažuriran pregledač za korišćenje. Testiran je na Android Chrome-u i iOS Safari-ju, kao i na Chrome-u i Firefox-u na računaru."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:250
msgid ""
"The server is careful to use functionality that has either been already "
"standardised or is on the standards track. As such if it does not currently "
"work with your favorite browser, it probably will once that browser has "
"caught up."
msgstr "Server pažljivo koristi funkcionalnost koja je ili već standardizovana ili je na putu standardizacije. Kao takav, ako trenutno ne radi sa vašim omiljenim pregledačem, verovatno će raditi kada taj pregledač uhvati korak."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:255
msgid ""
"If you are using a particularly old or limited browser or you don't like to "
"run JavaScript, you can use the *mobile* view, by simply adding ``/mobile`` "
"to the server address."
msgstr "Ako koristite posebno star ili ograničen pregledač ili ne želite da pokrećete JavaScript, možete koristiti *mobile* prikaz, jednostavnim dodavanjem ``/mobile`` na adresu servera."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:260
msgid ""
"On iOS, Apple allows only a single browser engine, so Firefox, Chrome and "
"Safari are all actually the same browser under the hood. The new server "
"interface requires iOS 10.3.2 or newer. On Android, the server has been "
"tested with Chrome version 58 and newer."
msgstr "Na iOS-u, Apple dozvoljava samo jedan endžin pregledača, tako da su Firefox, Chrome i Safari zapravo isti pregledač ispod haube. Novi interfejs servera zahteva iOS 10.3.2 ili noviji. Na Androidu, server je testiran sa Chrome verzijom 58 i novijim."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:266
msgid "Enabling offline support"
msgstr "Omogućavanje oflajn podrške"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:268
msgid ""
"The server has full support for offline mode, you can open a book and once "
"it is loaded, continue reading it offline. However, typical browsers require"
" the use of HTTPS connections to enable offline mode (service workers). So "
":ref:`setup HTTPS support <cs_https_mode>` as described above. Scroll to the"
" bottom of the home page and you will see a message about the status of "
"offline mode."
msgstr "Server ima punu podršku za oflajn režim, možete otvoriti knjigu i kada se učita, nastaviti da je čitate oflajn. Međutim, tipični pregledači zahtevaju upotrebu HTTPS konekcija da bi omogućili oflajn režim (service workers). Zato :ref:`podesite HTTPS podršku <cs_https_mode>` kao što je opisano iznad. Pomerite se do dna početne stranice i videćete poruku o statusu oflajn režima."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:275
msgid ""
"Alternately, you can open a book and keep the browser tab open. As long as "
"the tab stays open you can continue reading the book, even when offline."
msgstr "Alternativno, možete otvoriti knjigu i ostaviti karticu pregledača otvorenom. Sve dok kartica ostaje otvorena, možete nastaviti da čitate knjigu, čak i kada ste oflajn."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:279
msgid "Managing user accounts from the command-line only"
msgstr "Upravljanje korisničkim nalozima samo iz komandne linije"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:281
msgid ""
"The calibre program has a nice section in :guilabel:`Preferences` to allow "
"you to manage user accounts for the server. However, if you want to run the "
"standalone server and cannot run the main calibre program on the same "
"computer/user account, you can also manage users using just the command-"
"line."
msgstr "Program calibre ima odeljak u :guilabel:`Preferences` koja vam omogućava da upravljate korisničkim nalozima za server. Međutim, ako želite da pokrenete samostalni server i ne možete da pokrenete glavni calibre program na istom računaru/korisničkom nalogu, možete takođe upravljati korisnicima koristeći samo komandnu liniju."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:286
msgid ""
"You can manage user accounts using the ``--manage-users`` option to the "
"standalone ``calibre-server`` program. Suppose you want to store the user "
"database in the folder ``/srv/calibre``, then you create it by running::"
msgstr "Možete upravljati korisničkim nalozima koristeći opciju ``--manage-users`` za samostalni program ``calibre-server``. Pretpostavimo da želite da sačuvate bazu korisnika u fascikli ``/srv/calibre``, onda je kreirate pokretanjem::"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:293
msgid ""
"Just follow the prompts to create user accounts, set their permissions, etc."
" Once you are done, you can run the server as::"
msgstr "Samo pratite uputstva da kreirate korisničke naloge, postavite njihove dozvole, itd. Kada završite, možete pokrenuti server kao::"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:298
msgid "It will use the user accounts you created in the previous step."
msgstr "Koristiće korisničke naloge koje ste kreirali u prethodnom koraku."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:301
msgid "Syncing reading progress with KOReader"
msgstr "Sinhronizacija napretka čitanja sa KOReader-om"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:303
msgid ""
"The Content server can act as a progress sync server for the `KOReader "
"<https://koreader.rocks>`_ e-book reader, so that devices running KOReader "
"can sync your reading position in books with each other. In KOReader, go to "
":guilabel:`Tools->Progress sync->Custom sync server` and enter the address "
"of the Content server followed by ``/kosync``, for example::"
msgstr "Server sadržaja može služiti kao server za sinhronizaciju napretka čitanja za pregledač e-knjiga `KOReader <https://koreader.rocks>`_, tako da uređaji na kojima se koristi KOReader mogu međusobno da sinhronizuju vaš položaj čitanja u knjigama. U KOReader-u otvorite :guilabel:`Alatke->Sinhronizacija napretka->Prilagođeni server za sinhronizaciju` i unesite adresu servera sadržaja, a zatim ``/kosync``, na primer::"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:311
msgid ""
"If you are `Using a URL prefix`_, include it before ``/kosync``. Then use "
":guilabel:`Login` with the username and password of a user account on the "
"Content server. Accounts cannot be created from KOReader, they are managed "
"by calibre as described above. Users that are only allowed read access "
"cannot sync their reading positions. If user accounts are not enabled on the"
" server, any username and password can be used, but reading positions can "
"only be synced from devices that are allowed to make changes without "
"authentication, see the :guilabel:`Allow un-authenticated local connections "
"to make changes` and :guilabel:`Allow un-authenticated connections from "
"specific IP addresses to make changes` options. Reading positions synced "
"while user accounts are not enabled are kept separate from those of user "
"accounts. The reading positions of each user are stored separately in the "
"user database of the server."
msgstr "Ako koristite URL prefiks, kao što je opisano u odeljku `Korišćenje URL prefiksa`_, navedite ga ispred ``/kosync``. Zatim koristite :guilabel:`Prijava` sa korisničkim imenom i lozinkom korisničkog naloga na serveru sadržaja. Nalozi se ne mogu praviti iz KOReader-a; njima upravlja calibre, kao što je opisano iznad. Korisnici koji imaju samo pravo čitanja ne mogu sinhronizovati položaje čitanja. Ako korisnički nalozi nisu omogućeni na serveru, može se koristiti bilo koje korisničko ime i lozinka, ali se položaji čitanja mogu sinhronizovati samo sa uređaja kojima je dozvoljeno da prave izmene bez autentifikacije; pogledajte opcije :guilabel:`Dozvoli lokalnim vezama bez autentifikacije da prave izmene` i :guilabel:`Dozvoli vezama sa određenih IP adresa da prave izmene bez autentifikacije`. Položaji čitanja sinhronizovani dok korisnički nalozi nisu omogućeni čuvaju se odvojeno od položaja korisničkih naloga. Položaji čitanja svakog korisnika čuvaju se zasebno u bazi korisnika servera."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:324
msgid ""
"By default, KOReader identifies books by a checksum of the book file. The "
"Content server can change the metadata embedded in books when they are "
"downloaded, so copies of a book downloaded at different times can have "
"different checksums. Once KOReader has synced with the server, it remembers "
"the checksums of downloaded books and of the library files they were created"
" from, so that all copies of the same format of a book share one reading "
"position. Different formats of a book have separate reading positions, as "
"positions in one format cannot be used in another. Copies downloaded before "
"KOReader first synced with the server, or obtained other than by downloading"
" them from the server, are not recognized. If reading positions do not sync "
"for such copies, set :guilabel:`Document matching method` in the KOReader "
"progress sync settings to :guilabel:`Filename` on all devices and keep the "
"file names of books the same."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:340
msgid "Integrating the calibre Content server into other servers"
msgstr "Integracija calibre Content servera u druge servere"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:342
msgid ""
"Here, we will show you how to integrate the calibre Content server into "
"another server. The most common reason for this is to make use of SSL or to "
"serve the calibre library as part of a larger site. The basic technique is "
"to run the calibre server and set up a reverse proxy to it from the main "
"server."
msgstr "Ovde ćemo vam pokazati kako da integrišete calibre Content server u drugi server. Najčešći razlog za to je korišćenje SSL-a ili omogućavanje pristupa calibre biblioteci preko većeg sajta. Osnovna tehnika je pokretanje calibre servera i postavljanje obrnutog proksija (reverse proxy) do njega sa glavnog servera."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:347
msgid ""
"A reverse proxy is when your normal server accepts incoming requests and "
"passes them onto the calibre server. It then reads the response from the "
"calibre server and forwards it to the client. This means that you can simply"
" run the calibre server as normal without trying to integrate it closely "
"with your main server."
msgstr "Obrnuti proksi je kada vaš glavni server prihvata dolazne zahteve i prosleđuje ih calibre serveru. Zatim čita odgovor sa calibre servera i prosleđuje ga klijentu. To znači da možete jednostavno pokrenuti calibre server kao i obično bez pokušaja da ga tesno povežete sa vašim glavnim serverom."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:354
msgid "Using a full virtual host"
msgstr "Korišćenje punog virtuelnog hosta"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:356
msgid ""
"The simplest configuration is to dedicate a full virtual host to the calibre"
" server. In this case, run the calibre server as::"
msgstr "Najjednostavnija konfiguracija je posvetiti pun virtuelni host calibre serveru. U ovom slučaju, pokrenite calibre server kao::"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:361
msgid ""
"Now setup the virtual host in your main server, for example, for nginx::"
msgstr "Sada postavite virtuelni host na vašem glavnom serveru, na primer, za nginx::"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:376
msgid "Or, for Apache::"
msgstr "Ili, za Apache::"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:391
msgid "Using a URL prefix"
msgstr "Korišćenje URL prefiksa"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:393
msgid ""
"If you do not want to dedicate a full virtual host to calibre, you can have "
"it use a URL prefix. Start the calibre server as::"
msgstr "Ako ne želite da posvetite pun virtuelni host za calibre, možete ga podesiti da koristi URL prefiks. Pokrenite calibre server kao::"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:398
msgid ""
"The key parameter here is ``--url-prefix /calibre``. This causes the Content"
" server to serve all URLs prefixed by ``/calibre``. To see this in action, "
"visit ``http://localhost:8080/calibre`` in your browser. You should see the "
"normal Content server website, but now it will run under ``/calibre``."
msgstr "Ključni parametar ovde je ``--url-prefix /calibre``. Ovo uzrokuje da Content server servira sve URL-ove sa prefiksom ``/calibre``. Da biste ovo videli na delu, posetite ``http://localhost:8080/calibre`` u vašem pregledaču. Trebalo bi da vidite normalan veb sajt Content servera, ali sada će raditi pod ``/calibre``."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:400
msgid "With nginx, the required configuration is::"
msgstr "Sa nginx-om, potrebna konfiguracija je::"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:417
msgid ""
"For Apache, first enable the proxy modules in Apache, by adding the "
"following to :file:`httpd.conf`::"
msgstr "Za Apache, prvo omogućite proxy module u Apache-u, dodavanjem sledećeg u :file:`httpd.conf`::"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:422
msgid ""
"The exact technique for enabling the proxy modules will vary depending on "
"your Apache installation. Once you have the proxy modules enabled, add the "
"following rules to :file:`httpd.conf` (or if you are using virtual hosts to "
"the conf file for the virtual host in question)::"
msgstr "Tačna tehnika za omogućavanje proxy modula će varirati u zavisnosti od vaše Apache instalacije. Kada omogućite proxy module, dodajte sledeća pravila u :file:`httpd.conf` (ili ako koristite virtuelne hostove u conf fajl za dotični virtuelni host)::"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:429
msgid ""
"That's all, you will now be able to access the calibre Content server under "
"the ``/calibre`` URL in your main server. The above rules pass all requests "
"under ``/calibre`` to the calibre server running on port 8080 and thanks to "
"the ``--url-prefix`` option above, the calibre server handles them "
"transparently."
msgstr "To je sve, sada ćete moći da pristupite calibre Content serveru pod ``/calibre`` URL-om na vašem glavnom serveru. Gore navedena pravila prosleđuju sve zahteve pod ``/calibre`` calibre serveru koji radi na portu 8080 i zahvaljujući opciji ``--url-prefix`` iznad, calibre server ih transparentno obrađuje."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:434
msgid ""
"When using a reverse proxy, you should tell the calibre Content server to "
"only listen on localhost, by using ``--listen-on 127.0.0.1``. That way, the "
"server will only listen for connections coming from the same computer, i.e. "
"from the reverse proxy."
msgstr "Kada koristite obrnuti proksi, trebalo bi da kažete calibre Content serveru da sluša samo na localhost-u, koristeći ``--listen-on 127.0.0.1``. Na taj način, server će slušati samo konekcije koje dolaze sa istog računara, tj. sa obrnutog proksija."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:441
msgid ""
"If you have set up SSL for your main server, you should tell the calibre "
"server to use basic authentication instead of digest authentication, as it "
"is faster. To do so, pass the ``--auth-mode=basic`` option to ``calibre-"
"server``."
msgstr "Ako ste podesili SSL za vaš glavni server, trebalo bi da kažete calibre serveru da koristi osnovnu autentifikaciju umesto digest autentifikacije, jer je brža. Da biste to uradili, prosledite opciju ``--auth-mode=basic`` komandi ``calibre-server``."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:450
msgid "Creating a service for the calibre server on a modern Linux system"
msgstr "Pravljenje servisa za calibre server na savremenom Linux sistemu"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:452
msgid ""
"You can easily create a service to run calibre at boot on a modern (`systemd"
" <https://www.freedesktop.org/wiki/Software/systemd/>`_) based Linux system."
" Just create the file ``/etc/systemd/system/calibre-server.service`` with "
"the contents shown below::"
msgstr "Možete lako kreirati servis za pokretanje calibre-a pri pokretanju na savremenom Linux sistemu zasnovanom na `systemd <https://www.freedesktop.org/wiki/Software/systemd/>`_. Samo kreirajte fajl ``/etc/systemd/system/calibre-server.service`` sa sadržajem prikazanim ispod::"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:471
msgid ""
"Change ``mylinuxuser`` and ``mylinuxgroup`` to whatever user and group you "
"want the server to run as. This should be the same user and group that own "
"the files in the calibre library folder. Note that it is generally not a "
"good idea to run the server as root. Also change the path to the calibre "
"library folder to suit your system. You can add multiple libraries if "
"needed. See the help for the ``calibre-server`` command."
msgstr "Promenite ``mylinuxuser`` i ``mylinuxgroup`` u korisnika i grupu pod kojima želite da se server pokreće. Ovo bi trebalo da bude isti korisnik i grupa koji poseduju fajlove u folderu calibre biblioteke. Imajte na umu da generalno nije dobra ideja pokretati server kao root. Takođe promenite putanju do foldera calibre biblioteke da odgovara vašem sistemu. Možete dodati više biblioteka ako je potrebno. Pogledajte pomoć za komandu ``calibre-server``."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:478
msgid "Now run::"
msgstr "Sada pokrenite::"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:482
msgid "to start the server. Check its status with::"
msgstr "da biste pokrenuli server. Proverite njegov status sa::"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:486
msgid "To make it start at boot, run::"
msgstr "Da biste ga podesili da se pokreće pri pokretanju sistema, pokrenite::"

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:492
msgid ""
"The calibre server *does not* need a running X server, but it does need the "
"X libraries installed as some components it uses link against them."
msgstr "calibre server *ne zahteva* pokrenut X server, ali zahteva instalirane X biblioteke jer se neke komponente koje koristi povezuju sa njima."

#: ../../../__w/calibre/calibre/manual/server.rst:497
msgid ""
"The calibre server also supports systemd socket activation, so you can use "
"that, if needed, as well."
msgstr "calibre server takođe podržava systemd aktivaciju soketa, tako da i to možete koristiti, ako je potrebno."
